description.narrative:
The objective of the CHSS Phase II project is to strengthen research capabilities of scholars and local institutions in humanities and social sciences, particularly among under-represented scholars and local institutions in marginalized communities and regions where academic resources are most limited. By fostering their knowledge production, critical analysis and research skills, the CHSS project will contribute to reducing social and economic vulnerabilities in low and lower middle-income countries across South and Southeast Asia, especially in post-conflict and conflict areas.

The main objective will be achieved through these interventions:
i) strengthening research capacity at local universities by enhancing the academic knowledge, research skills, and resources of scholars in the humanities and social sciences, with a focus on junior faculty, graduate students, independent scholars, women, and ethnic minority groups;
ii) supporting academic institutions and building sustainable research environments;
iii) generating policy relevant research in conflict affected areas that addresses social and economic vulnerabilities in the region; 
iv) and equipping scholars and institutions with the analytical tools needed to contribute to civil society and policy development. 

Through these interventions, CHSS will continue to empower under resourced universities to host research activities, build institutional capacity, and nurture a new generation of homegrown scholars capable of advancing peacebuilding, cooperation, and development across underserved regions.
